description:
Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts using a REPLACE operation on an existing file. Do not use create_file: that file already exists and is about 181000 bytes, and a create_file op will be refused.

Perform exactly one replacement. The old_string is these three lines, which occur exactly once in the file (six spaces before continue, four before the closing brace, four before actionableGaps):

      continue;
    }
    actionableGaps.push(g);

The new_string is these two lines, identical except that the `continue;` line is gone:

    }
    actionableGaps.push(g);

That is the entire change. Do not comment the line out — an earlier attempt added a comment beside it and was correctly rejected by the semantic gate as "zero behaviour delta". Do not anchor on a bare `continue;`, which occurs twice in this file. Do not trust any line number; this file shifts as other changes land.

Purpose: this `continue` sits inside the `if (hopeless(g))` branch of pickMostLandable and drops every gap in a hopeless category before scoring runs, so 23 documentation_drift gaps that already compute to the joint top landability of 1.00 are never selected. Removing it lets them fall through to actionableGaps and be scored, which is the "re-test path (penalty, not hard exclusion)" the comment above hopeless() already promises. Keep the uiQuestion_write escalation exactly as it is. Do not alter hopeless(), landabilityScore, or any threshold, and introduce no new symbol.

